a.c('qualification_lanes','Qualification lanes','Smoke asserts protocol completion (response exists/judge ran), not artifact quality. Qualification asserts judge pass and serves as release gate; shared-state entropy campaigns are separate from fresh-sandbox qualification.',[g(0,78,90)])
a.q('qualification_run_count',['qualification_lanes'],'Statistical-confidence questions declare/parameterize independent run count as named constant and state supported population. A bounded deterministic/installed/live steel-thread gate may declare one run when only exact scenario completion is claimed; 5.0 does not claim generic pass@k. Entropy campaigns still require artifact integrity without fallback masking.',[g(0,82,90)])
a.c('persistent_run_archive','Persistent scenario archive','Stable nontemporary immutable per-scenario/use-case and sortable-timestamp archive preserves live qualification material for postmortem, not merely execution scratch or test internals.',[g(1,96,108),g(1,123,127)])
a.q('archive_live_evidence',['persistent_run_archive'],'Every live qualification archives dispatch manifest, actual prompt/raw response, judged artifact, per-criterion judge verdict, model and transport before assertions. Selected installed-path archive retains exact source/artifact identities, requests/results, relevant worksite changes, native process/command observations, event-resource identity and genuine readback/close receipts where produced; missing terminal evidence stays explicit, without requiring historical directory names or irrelevant caches.',[g(1,96,116)])
a.q('archive_metadata_and_lifetime',['persistent_run_archive'],'Path encodes test/scenario/Run/time, navigable use-case first then run. Metadata includes timestamp, test identity, source commit, interpreter and commands; summary includes convergence, failing evaluators and key artifacts; subprocess stdout/stderr captured when applicable. Each new immutable non-overwriting path preserves prior archives; materialization completes before cleanup/teardown or temporary-directory deletion.',[g(1,106,127)])
a.c('installed_qualification','Installed substrate qualification','Proving obligations over REQ-P-INSTALL require downstream sandboxes claiming installed truth to use public ABG installer, retaining inspectable package/manifest/command/runtime/root truth and persistent proof.',[g(2,133,141)])
a.q('installer_proof_surface',['installed_qualification'],'Source imports/private helpers/harness-only bindings are insufficient installed closure proof. Installer writes package identity, installer/install manifest paths, command paths, runtime identity, event/projection roots and execution package root. Persistent archive includes manifests/package/commands/runtime/event-projection evidence and operator postmortem.',[g(2,137,141)])
a.r('installed_evidence_archived','requires','installed_qualification','persistent_run_archive','Installer qualification preserves persistent postmortem under stable test-run archive root.',[g(2,141)],governing=True)
a.c('diff_execution_witness','Diff-execution witness','Approval includes attributable changed-behavior execution and affected owning boundaries, including meaningful nearest negatives, at proof level matching the claim.',[g(3,147,153)])
a.q('proof_claim_boundary',['diff_execution_witness','installed_qualification'],'Component checks do not establish installed outcomes; exports or blanket coverage of never-committed files do not establish behavior. Installed Product qualification executes packed-and-installed ordinary surface; source checks stay narrower. Historical exemption counts, private legacy APIs and migration tickets neither define qualification nor excuse missing installed evidence.',[g(3,147,153),g(4,157,161)])
a.l('exact_evidence_reuse',['diff_execution_witness'],['Reuse still-valid exact-subject evidence with scope and identity.'],['Hide unexercised material changes; they remain explicit limitations.'],[g(3,147,153)])
a.c('development_rc_preview','Unqualified development RC1 preview','Owner/operator external preview under Product owner 2026-10-30 direction is explicitly unqualified, not AF-25/release.snapshot output or completed S07.',[g(5,167,174)])
a.q('preview_no_qualification_credit',['development_rc_preview'],'Record source/artifact/install identity, declared claim, known gaps and actual mechanical checks without invented green verdict. Native green snapshot/final acceptance law is unchanged; preview gives no credit for missing qualification.',[g(5,167,174)])
a.c('release_snapshot_bundle','Qualified immutable RC snapshot bundle','Release-process output records already-qualified published RC cut; later tap reports same unchanged cut, never live constitutional version truth or an input to its own qualification.',[g(5,176,186)])
a.q('snapshot_gate_and_identity',['release_snapshot_bundle'],'AF-25/release.snapshot creates one immutable versioned package-first RC cut/bundle only after exact same-subject/same-law green non-bypassed pre_rc_candidate verdict. tapped_release reports qualification and actual human acceptance of unchanged RC, not another cut/snapshot. Creation fails closed for dirty source, mismatched requested/package identity or populated target root; package explicit source root/ref, never reinterpret mutable checkout as tagged release.',[g(5,181,186),g(5,199,208)])
a.q('snapshot_artifact_evidence',['release_snapshot_bundle'],'Bundle includes at least tarball, manifest, checksum file, existing release-note copy, package identity, source ref/commit, build/pack commands and verification facts. Record deterministic tarball/generated-file checksums. Manifest is authoritative artifact-set read model; stray tarballs/dry-run pack/notes/snapshot cannot replace basis, authenticated assessments or authorizing verdict.',[g(5,188,204)])
a.q('snapshot_not_evaluator',['release_snapshot_bundle'],'Bounded self-certifying read model embeds exact subject/law refs, complete assessments/execution citations, green non-bypassed verdict, build/lint/test outcomes and parsed summary; never executes or reinterprets gates. Red/incomplete/stale/cross-basis/bypassed refuses release-grade cut. Explicit non-release snapshot may honor declared bypasses only with null evidence and never green/promotable representation.',[g(5,210,218)])
a.l('nonrelease_snapshot_bypass',['release_snapshot_bundle'],['Honor declared bypass booleans only for explicitly non-release snapshot, recording null evidence.'],['Represent bypassed gates as green/promotable or admit release-grade bypasses.'],[g(5,210,218)])
